From f673c6690520f55f78013cda98b67d8ec2534c79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:59:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 22/58] usb: dwc3: apple: Add the bare-metal T6050 controller

Add apple,t6050-dwc3, the T6050 (J775D) DWC3 on bare metal. It uses the
shared tunable table, extended with the tables Diljit Singh's T6050 USB
support applies, in the same order: the T6040 tables plus CIO (the Apple
region from 0xcd20, after the fixed CIO values), bulk fabric and AUSBC
debug (the optional drd-bulk and drd-ausbc regions).

It is host-only, like T6040. The USB2 port reset follows the root hub's
start (a no-op without a PHY reset op), and a USB3 PHY failure is fatal,
as on T8132.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/usb/apple,dwc3.yaml   | 40 +++++++-
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c                 | 95 +++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 112 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

